{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-43974",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The expression $6z+\\frac{3}{2}x+2y+\\frac{5}{2}$ has four terms:  $6z$, $\\frac{3}{2}x$, $2y$ and $\\frac{5}{2}.$ \n\nThe order in which we combine the terms doesn't matter. Therefore, we can also write this expression as \n\n$$\n2y+\\frac{5}{2}+6z+\\frac{3}{2}x.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
